George Pell is the most senior Roman  Catholic Church figure anywhere in the  world to be jailed for child sex  offenses in 2018 he was convicted of  abusing two thirteen-year-old choir boys  in the late 90s and given a six year  jail sentence  now he's appealing to Australia's  highest court to have that conviction  overturned his lawyers argued too much  weight was placed on the credibility of  Pels accuser and not enough on other  witnesses and after losing an appeal  last year this is his final chance to  clear his name and be released from  prison it's very hard but if these  things in particular it's hard to  predict where four of the seven judges  will go but he's certainly going into  Tuesday with a good chance of being  freed he'll was a priest in rural  Australia before quickly rising through  the ranks from Archbishop of Melbourne  and Sydney to a cardinal in charge of  the Vatican's finances campaigners for  sexual abuse victims are worried if he  does walk free it may stop others from  speaking out I think that there is  definitely the potential for is to have  a devastating impact on many who may not  many who may lose faith in the criminal  justice system the ruling is being  delivered in the middle of the most  important week in the Catholic calendar  when 1.3 billion members celebrate  Easter if Paul's conviction is  overturned he could walk free from  prison within hours  Pell has continued to maintain his  innocence but whatever the court decides  its findings will be significant  bringing to an end a five-year long  legal saga that millions have been  following across the world Nicola gage  al Jazeera Sydney
 

